      "hints": [
        "Combine fractions on the LHS over $(1 + \\cos\\theta)(1 - \\cos\\theta) = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "Expand numerator to $2\\tan\\theta$.",
        "Replace $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and simplify to $\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Combine the two terms on the LHS over their common denominator:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{\\tan\\theta(1 - \\cos\\theta) + \\tan\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)}{(1 + \\cos\\theta)(1 - \\cos\\theta)}$$",
        "Expand and simplify the numerator:\n$$\\text{Numerator} = \\tan\\theta - \\tan\\theta\\cos\\theta + \\tan\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\cos\\theta = 2\\tan\\theta$$",
        "Simplify the denominator using the Pythagorean identity $1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$:\n$$\\text{Denominator} = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$$",
        "Substitute $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and cancel a factor of $\\sin\\theta$:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{2\\left(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)}{\\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{2\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
